WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.240
David Ayer would like to be left out of this
whole Joker mess, thank you very much.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.540
The Suicide Squad director took to Twitter
to defend himself in the wake of a report

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:15.190
that Jared Leto's role as the Joker in Suicide
Squad was severely reduced because Ayer was

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.160
unhappy with his performance.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.960
It's just the latest development in a strange
drama that has played out after the success

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.760
of Joker, the hit origin story starring Joaquin
Phoenix.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.220
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Leto
was none too thrilled when Warner Bros. put

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.580
a solo Joker film into production that did
not star him, after Suicide Squad made nearly

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.220
$750 million dollars at the global box office.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.860
Leto famously committed to the role; some
people, like his co-stars, might say he was

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:49.730
a little too committed, with the actors reportedly
being gifted rats, bullets, and dead pigs

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.600
as part of Leto's "method" approach to playing
the Joker.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.900
But Leto's depiction of the Joker left many
DC fans unimpressed.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.820
The fact that Leto's screen time was limited
to only about ten minutes in Suicide Squad's

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.780
final cut probably ended up benefiting the
film.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.020
But if the quality of the actor's performance
had anything to do with that decision, the

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.280
director isn't coming clean about it.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.880
In response to a fan who asked him on Twitter
if the report was true, Ayer simply responded,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.640
"This is inaccurate information.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.190
Not my words or actions."

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.900
THR's reporting has detailed how Leto was
upset over Joaquin Phoenix's Joker movie being

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:31.910
put into development before either of his
own Joker-centric projects - a solo movie

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:36.420
for his Joker, and a team-up with Margot Robbie's
Harley Quinn - had come to pass.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:41.140
He reportedly fumed about the situation to
his agents, and allegedly went so far as to

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:46.549
ask one of his well-connected buddies - Irving
Azoff, his music manager - to put in a call

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:50.880
to Warner Bros. brass in an attempt to get
Phoenix's Joker killed.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.520
"Do it.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.160
Do it do it do it do"

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.620
Joker, of course, has gone on to make roughly
all of the money, while becoming the most

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.310
talked-about film of the fall.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.600
Meanwhile, both films set to feature his Joker
are now apparently dead in the water.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.560
The latest trailer for 2020's Birds of Prey
opens with Harley Quinn stating flatly that

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.560
she dumped the Joker, just as unceremoniously
as Warner Bros. appears to have done.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.580
So, what are the chances that Leto will eventually
return to the role?

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:23.200
Well, nothing's official yet, and it's worth
noting that Leto still maintains a professional

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:27.260
relationship with Warner Bros, and is currently
shooting the crime thriller Little Things

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.360
for the studio.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.760
That said, we're definitely thinking that
Leto's turn as the Joker will prove to be

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.320
a one-and-done.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.880
With Joaquin Phoenix's Joker movie also being
widely described as a standalone project,

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.260
it's possible the next time we see the Joker,
it will be a whole new actor under the makeup.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.440
But no matter who eventually gets recast as
the Joker, we know one thing: it's gotta happen

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.440
eventually.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.780
"I think you and I are destined to do this
forever."

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.600
Assuming Jared Leto doesn't sneakily show
up in Birds of Prey somehow, it seems possible

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.120
that the next iteration of the character won't
happen until we get a sequel to Matt Reeves'

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.700
The Batman, set to hit theaters in 2021.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.220
That movie, starring Robert Pattinson in the
lead role, seems to be packing its cast with

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.860
tons of villains from Batman's Rogues' Gallery.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.700
But so far, we've heard nothing about a Joker
appearance.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:23.200
With no other movies featuring the character
having been announced yet, it looks like the

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.060
live-action Joker might be resting for awhile.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:31.120
But he's not necessarily done with comic book
movies, with his turn as Morbius, the Living

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.320
Vampire set to debut in Sony's Marvel universe
in 2020.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:40.420
So as long as he can keep from mailing dead
bats to his co-stars on that movie, he should

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.920
get along just fine.

